  "scope": "The main application keeps the graph-theoretic asymptotic and the finite Lindemann-Weierstrass input as explicit hypotheses. Passing does not prove those two external theorems. OrderedCancellation verifies the abstract filtered ring and finite-packet recursion only; it does not formalize tournament kernel costs, permanent recovery, or Condition R. ColorEnergy verifies finite prefix-energy algebra only. ColorTransport proves actual word reachability and an area lower bound, not optimal area attainment or graph-edit bounds. DiamondGap proves only finite tournament diamond coverage and D=0 or n<=4D; this does not imply Condition R."
